# VOYAGE -- family: JOURNEY.
# Idea: TRIP is a road through five leads. Osc 1's wave and the filter type
# are enums and can only jump, so every wave jump sits where osc 2 (a sine an
# octave up) swells in and covers it: the oscillator mix rises to a peak at
# each jump and falls back at each station (all four jumps: round 1 could not
# cover the last one, at 0.875, with the 8 points a v1 curve allowed).
#   0.00 FLUTE   triangle, soft and breathy, sine on top
#   0.25 LEAD    saw lead, resonant low-pass, snappy envelope
#   0.50 HOLLOW  narrow pulse through a band-pass, nasal
#   0.75 SUPER   supersaw, open and wide
#   1.00 METAL   FM 2 through a high-pass, thin and glassy
# GRIT and SPACE are spice for any station.
# audit: allow-jump TRIP
# Feel if it works: you travel between instruments while a line plays and the
# trip itself is music; the in-between places are not broken.
# Try: TRIP on X, GRIT on Y; hold a chord and walk TRIP from 0 to 1 over
# eight bars.
voice lead
name VOYAGE
about "From flute to metal in one sweep."
base env=34 osc2=sine intv=36 det=40 attack=4 decay=80 release=46 fatk=0 fdcy=56 ktrk=64 vib=10 lfo=96 glide=50

macro TRIP
  wave     0:tri 0.125:saw 0.375:puls 0.625:supr 0.875:fm2
  flt      0:lp 0.44:bp 0.6:lp 0.875:hp       # band-pass only where the cutoff is down near the notes
  mix      0:40 0.125:105 0.25:50 0.375:105 0.5:30 0.625:105 0.75:40 0.875:105 1:20 smooth
  cutoff   0:62 0.25:92 0.5:40 0.75:100 0.875:54 1:60 smooth   # a band-pass is loud only near the notes
  reso     0:10 0.25:42 0.5:26 0.75:20 1:56 smooth      # ... and with a wide band
  lvl      0:102 0.25:100 0.375:116 0.5:122 0.625:104 0.75:100 0.875:116 1:110 smooth   # BP and HP lose level
  shape    0:0 0.25:20 0.5:84 0.75:84 1:96 smooth
  sus      0:96 0.25:72 0.5:40 0.75:84 1:30 smooth

macro GRIT
  drive    0:0 1:100
  reso     add 0:0 1:20
  env      add 0:0 1:20
  lvl      add 0:0 1:-8

macro SPACE
  dly      0:10 1:90
  rev      0:24 1:100
  release  add 0:0 1:40
  cutoff   add 0:0 1:-10      # far away is a little darker
